---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "knowledge networks — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>knowledge networks</h1>
    <p>a knowledge network isn't just what you know; it's the structure of how you know it. strong networks have multiple pathways to the same idea (you can reach "systems thinking" via complexity theory, business, ecology, neurology). weak networks are linear: you know a leads to b, but little else.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>strong networks have redundancy: multiple routes to each idea</li>
      <li>build them by learning the same concept through different sources</li>
      <li>add weak links (surprising connections): they're the most valuable</li>
      <li>periodically review and reorganize your network as it grows</li>
      <li>teach others; explaining reveals gaps in your network</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="care">a dense network is more resilient. if you forget one path to an idea, you have others.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
